   Enables BGP multipath load balancing for up to 8 paths (both EBGP and IBGP), allowing installation of multiple next-hops in the routing table.

2. **`ibgp-multipath`**  
   Ensures IBGP routes can use multiple next-hops when resolving BGP nexthops, critical for route reflection environments.

3. **`add-paths ipv4 send 8 receive`**  
   - `send 8`: Advertises up to 8 distinct paths per IPv4 prefix to peers  
   - `receive`: Requests peers to send multiple paths per prefix (negotiates BGP add-paths capability)

### Important Notes:
- Replace `<your_group_name>` and `<neighbor_IP>` with your actual BGP group and neighbor IP
- Ensure IPv4 family is already enabled under the neighbor configuration
- Both peers must support BGP add-paths (RFC 7911) for this to work
- Path selection still follows standard BGP best-path rules before multipath consideration
- No impact on route reflection functionality when configured as shown

These commands allow advertising multiple diverse next-hops for the same prefix while requesting the same from peers, enabling traffic engineering via alternate paths without MPLS.
