"On a Nokia 7750 SR, during those extended restart scenarios where peers take longer to recover, how do I make sure the router uses our own 5-minute timer for every address family the peer lists as restart-capable, instead of relying on their advertised values?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure the router uses a 5-minute (300-second) timer for all restart-capable address families, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            helper-override-restart-time 300
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This command overrides the peer's advertised restart timer with your locally configured value (300 seconds) for all address families supported by the peer during graceful restarts.
