To configure your 7750 SR to pass VPNv4 routes over an IPv6 BGP session while preserving the peer's IPv6 next-hop, apply the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        family vpn-ipv4
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4
        group "SITE-A"
            peer-as <AS_A>
            neighbor <SITE_A_IPv6>
                family vpn-ipv4
                next-hop-unchanged
            exit
        exit
        group "SITE-B"
            peer-as <AS_B>
            neighbor <SITE_B_IPv6>
                family vpn-ipv4
                next-hop-unchanged
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key Configuration Notes:
1. **`family vpn-ipv4`**:  
   Enables VPNv4 route exchange globally and per neighbor.

2. **`advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4`**:  
   Forces VPNv4 routes to use an IPv6 next-hop over the IPv6 transport session.

3. **`next-hop-unchanged`**:  
