To ensure BGP holds onto IPv6 paths during a neighbor's control plane reboot (e.g., software upgrade) without tearing down sessions, configure Graceful Restart (GR) helper functionality and Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) with appropriate timers. Replace `"<group-name>"` and `"<neighbor-ipv6_address>"` with your specific values.

### Configuration Commands:
```cli
# Enable global BGP Graceful Restart helper
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 600          # Advertise 10-min recovery window (default: 300s)
        long-lived                # Enable LLGR to retain stale paths beyond restart-time
        enable-notification       # Allow session preservation on NOTIFICATION messages
    exit
exit

